<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="diaMuertos-ws-setsAmongUs">
  <title>SETS Among Us</title>
    
    <introduction>
      <sidebyside widths="50% 35%" margins="0% 5%" valign="middle">
        <p><paragraphs>
        <title>Start</title>
        <p>Brainstorm <q>people</q> aspects. Write each in 1 index card. Example: <term>FAVORITE MUSIC</term>. What are some possible options or values for each?</p>
        <p>Focus on non-binary aspects! (More than 2 options or values).</p>
      </paragraphs></p>
        <!-- <image source="diaMuertos-setsAmongUS-people1.png" decorative="yes"/> -->
        <image source="diaMuertos-setsAmongUS-people2.png" decorative="yes"/>
      </sidebyside>     
      
    </introduction>   

    <exercise xml:id="ex-sets-challenge1">
      <title>Challenge #1: One Aspect Only</title>
      <statement>
        <sidebyside widths="65% 25%" margins="0% 5%" valign="middle">
          <p>Do this together as a group:
          <ul>
            <li><p>Pick one aspect randomly. Example: <term>FAVORITE MUSIC</term></p></li>
            <li><p>Everyone talk about the aspect. Share.</p></li>
            <li><p>Select 2 random people in your table. Call it A and B.</p></li>
            <li><p>A and B tell us the <q>values</q> of the aspect. Are they equal or different?</p></li>
            <li><p>Together, find a third person C that would complete a <term>SET</term> with A and B. This means: <alert>either all three values are equal, or all three values are different</alert>. See the figure.</p></li>
            <li><p>Can you find other <term>SET</term>s as a group (with any 3 people in the table)?</p></li>
          </ul>
          </p>
          <stack>
            <image source="diaMuertos-set.png">
              <shortdescription>Two possible forms for a SET: all values equal or all values different.</shortdescription>
            </image>
            <p>Example of a SET</p>
          </stack>
        </sidebyside>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
    
    <exercise xml:id="ex-sets-challenge2" workspace="5cm">
      <title>Challenge #2: Three Aspects</title>
      <statement>
        <p>Do the same for 3 aspects at the same time. Example:
          <md>\boxed{\text{Favorite music}} + \boxed{\text{Month you were born}} + \boxed{\text{Favorite Weekend Family Activity}} </md>
        </p>
        <!-- <p>Favorite music + Month you were born + Favorite Weekend Family Activity</p> -->
        
        <p>A <term>SET</term> is a collection of 3 people such that:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>For the first aspect, all people's values are equal, or all values are different!</p></li>
          <li><p>For the second aspect, all people's values are equal, or all values are different!</p></li>
          <li><p>For the third aspect, all people's values are equal, or all values are different!</p></li>
        </ul>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
  </worksheet>
